{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:0.2", "PA_ja_20:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Sīlavagga (The Chapter on Virtue)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:0.4"], "en": "10. The Naḷapāna Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:1.1", "PA_ja_20:1.2"], "en": "“Having seen a footprint that has not crossed over, and having seen a footprint that has not descended;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:1.3"], "en": "“We shall drink water through a reed;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:1.4", "PA_ja_20:2.1"], "en": "you will not kill me. The *Naḷapāna Jātaka*, the tenth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:2.2"], "en": "The second chapter: On Virtue.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:3.1"], "en": "Its summary verse:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:4.1"], "en": "Now, Characteristics, Branches, and \"Woe be to you,\" again.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:4.2"], "en": "\"There are indeed no harsh sounds among tastes;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_20:4.3", "PA_ja_20:4.4"], "en": "it is better to drink the wind than to be released by one called a reed— ten [such instances] occur.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
